# alfe's CAD-side loader: a loaded file's (setq f ...) clobbers the loader's own F

Status: TODO
Priority: P2
Found: 2026-10-06, while writing protocol-alfe-load-forwards-open-write-ccs
(encoding-situations-cli-options section 6 point 5).

## Symptom

A file loaded through the bootstrap's source loader (alfe-load, and the
runtime's own load path that drives the same read loop) whose top-level code
does the most ordinary AutoLISP thing there is:

    (setq f (open "out.txt" "w"))
    (write-char 65 f)
    (close f)

fails on the NEXT read of the loop, under the hosted clautolisp engine:

    ERROR protocol request 1: AutoLISP builtin READ-LINE signaled an error:
    #<SB-SYS:FD-STREAM for "file .../out.txt"> is not a character input stream.

and the rest of the file is never read.

## Repro

autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp, %drive-open-ccs: change the
user file's variable names ccsfd1 / ccsfd2 back to f / g and run
protocol-alfe-load-forwards-open-write-ccs (needs clautolisp-sbcl built). The
first request (alfe-load ...) publishes DONE 1 FAIL with the message above.

## Cause

AutoLISP is dynamically scoped. autolisp-source-load-run-body-impl
(autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/autolisp-bootstrap.lsp) declares its locals
as ordinary names -- (/ f line line-no form-text form-start-line result
form-read defun-name eval-result capture-old piece piece-end) -- and evaluates
each user form INSIDE that dynamic extent. A user (setq f ...) therefore
assigns the loader's binding of F (the source file descriptor), and the loop's
next (read-line f) reads the user's output file. Same for LINE, RESULT, PIECE,
... Every CAD (AutoCAD, BricsCAD) has the same dynamic scope, so this is not
clautolisp-specific; the other loader helpers (alfe-load: PREV, RESULT;
autolisp-source-load-core-impl: RESOLVED, ...) have the same exposure.

## Fix direction

Give every local of the loader functions that are live while user code runs a
name no user program will use (an alfe-private prefix, e.g. __alfe-src-f),
and add a hosted test loading a file that setq's each common name (f, line,
result, path, prev) at top level.
